    <string name="home_sub_infinity" translatable="false">∞</string>
    <!-- No reader since the traffic readout began counting the term in days
         (home_sub_days_left). Kept, not deleted: it is the one phrasing for an
         absolute expiry the продукт has, and the next screen that needs one should
         find it rather than write a second. -->
    <string name="home_sub_expired">истекла</string>
    <!-- §4 puts the REMAINING TERM at the right end of the traffic readout, not an
         absolute date: «справа остаток срока («12 дн.»)», and the prototype's own
         demo state prints exactly «12 дн.». The wording is not invented for this
         line — «%1$d дн.» is already the product's way of saying a term in
         account_option_duration and buy_option_duration, so the readout, the price
         option and the renewal row all count days the same way.

         Why days and not the date the row used to print: this line is a readout that
         sits beside «4 ГБ / 10 ГБ» and answers the same question that pair does —
         how much is left — and a date makes the reader do the subtraction. The date
         still exists on the Аккаунт screen («Действует до …»), where the question is
         when the subscription ends rather than how much of it is left. -->
    <string name="home_sub_days_left">%1$d дн.</string>

